Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation (2026-08-29): the first review completed remotely but its response exceeded the MCP client's 300-second transport window. The retained sidecar was recovered via audit_trail and showed one blocker: use this repo's established .joe-janitor/ convention, not the generic skill's .rebar-janitor/ default. Revised Scope, plan, ACs, and file impact accordingly; also split the deterministic P6 compound criteria and made resumed-run coverage/idempotency behavior explicit. No repository audit work has started; the ticket remains open and unclaimed pending a signed PASS.","timestamp":1788034337423812746}],"created_at":1788033751824782278,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nRun the rebar-janitor codebase-health pipeline against the current rebar repository as a deliberate maintenance pause. This is a read-only audit of product code: the deliverables are durable audit artifacts, a human-approved remediation plan, and tracker tickets. No production or test code will be changed.\n\n## Scope\n\nInspect the repository for code debt, code and architectural smells, separation-of-concerns problems, spent optionality, documentation gaps, oversized units, weak test oracles, AI-generated-code and security smells, and temporal decay. Weight recently changed regions while covering the full codebase. Consult prior janitor artifacts, tickets, ADRs, and commit history so intentional decisions are not mistaken for defects.\n\nThis repository's established artifact location is `.joe-janitor/`: `docs/documentation-policy.md` explicitly recognizes that tree, and `.joe-janitor/tools.md` already contains the durable playbook. Reuse that location rather than the generic skill default.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Discovery: fan out one concern per independent agent, shard comment and test-suite review by subsystem, and pool path:line-cited findings without severity or confidence.\n2. Verification: independently blue-team each finding, establish reachable harm, check prior decisions and known-fine entries, apply the skill's fixed validity and impact floors, and persist the audit record plus reusable tool playbook.\n3. Remediation: obtain two blind proposals per survivor from asymmetric evidence bases (community practice versus project record), converge at move/end-state level, and research divergences.\n4. Approval: present the Remediation Plan one item at a time for human approve/refine/reject decisions; record explicit known-fine blessings only when given.\n5. Ticketization: first search for a matching current Janitor Cleanup epic and children; create only missing tracker records. Approved work becomes actionable child tickets with acceptance criteria, provenance, dependencies, and file impact.\n\nAny failed discovery shard remains an explicit coverage gap and prevents Phase 1 completion. Audit artifact updates preserve existing content and ticketization searches before creating records so a resumed run does not silently lose coverage or duplicate work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Discovery covers every concern required by the rebar-janitor skill.\n- [ ] Every discovery candidate has an exact path:line citation.\n- [ ] Discovery candidates contain no severity or confidence score.\n- [ ] Independent verification records validity for every candidate it processes.\n- [ ] Independent verification records impact and a reachable-harm statement for every candidate it processes.\n- [ ] Independent verification records prior-decision and known-fine handling.\n- [ ] Candidates below validity 0.75 are dropped.\n- [ ] Candidates below impact 0.5 are dropped.\n- [ ] The dated audit record is persisted at `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-29.md`.\n- [ ] The reusable command and pattern playbook is appended at `.joe-janitor/tools.md`.\n- [ ] The audit report records commands and tuned thresholds.\n- [ ] The audit report records survivors, dropped candidates, and their evidence-backed disposition.\n- [ ] Every surviving finding receives two blind asymmetric-evidence remediation proposals.\n- [ ] Every divergent proposal pair is researched before its item enters the Remediation Plan.\n- [ ] Each remediation item receives an explicit user approve, refine, or reject decision before ticket creation.\n- [ ] Approved work is filed as child tickets under a current Janitor Cleanup epic.\n- [ ] Each created child is linked back to this audit ticket.\n- [ ] No production code, tests, configuration, or documentation outside `.joe-janitor/` and the tracker is modified.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".joe-janitor/report-2026-08-29.md","reason":"Persist the verified audit record and approval/ticket outcomes in the repository's established janitor artifact tree."},{"path":".joe-janitor/tools.md","reason":"Append reusable read-only audit commands and tuned patterns to the existing playbook."},{"path":".joe-janitor/known-fine.md","reason":"Update only for explicit maintainer blessings during approval, if any."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7c850c7d-3097-4865-9d61-7f7f1caf54ea","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","audit","maintainability"],"ticket_id":"673c-f602-748b-4b90","ticket_type":"task","title":"Run codebase-health janitor audit — 2026-08-29","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d773c48f-18d9-42f4-875d-f22fbc75fe3f","73ef8bd2-8589-46dd-8275-556550a865d6","31d7d724-b753-4c32-9a46-a66e6cd8af77","a1dcf4cd-d9fd-4960-972f-a9c501213073","bf689d10-1a70-42b2-8c9c-113524d2df81","9423dbea-6c2a-426a-b893-ab84d8982bf9","7c850c7d-3097-4865-9d61-7f7f1caf54ea","3ff41a89-45d5-4b41-b8dc-6edb6975a5e4"]},"env_id"